CAT = "lituValues"; SEG = "VAL"
Q = [
("Which of these is one of the fundamental principles of British life?",
 "Individual liberty", ["Compulsory voting", "Military service", "Rule by royal decree"],
 "The handbook lists democracy, the rule of law, individual liberty, tolerance of those with different faiths and beliefs, and participation in community life. Voting is a right in the UK, not a legal duty."),
("Which of these is listed as a fundamental principle of British life?",
 "Tolerance of other faiths", ["Membership of a church", "Service in the armed forces", "Support for one party"],
 "Tolerance of those with different faiths and beliefs is one of the five principles. Nobody is required to belong to a church, serve in the forces or back a particular party."),
("In the citizenship pledge, new citizens promise to:",
 "Observe the UK's laws faithfully", ["Vote in every general election", "Join a recognised political party", "Serve on a jury every year"],
 "The pledge commits new citizens to respect the UK's rights and freedoms, uphold its democratic values, observe its laws faithfully and fulfil their duties as citizens. It says nothing about voting in every election or joining a party."),
("Which is a responsibility the handbook expects of everyone living in the UK?",
 "Look after the local environment", ["Join a local political party", "Attend a weekly religious service", "Take part in every local election"],
 "Residents are expected to look after the area they live in and the environment, obey the law, respect others' rights, treat others fairly and look after themselves and their families. Religious and political membership are personal choices."),
("Which freedom does the UK offer in return for residents meeting their responsibilities?",
 "Freedom of speech", ["Freedom from paying tax", "Exemption from jury service", "A guaranteed public job"],
 "The handbook lists freedom of belief and religion, freedom of speech, freedom from unfair discrimination, a right to a fair trial and a right to join in the election of a government. Everyone who earns enough still pays tax."),
("At a citizenship ceremony, new citizens swear or affirm allegiance to:",
 "The King", ["The Prime Minister", "Parliament", "Their local council"],
 "New citizens take an oath or affirmation of allegiance to the monarch and make the citizenship pledge. Since September 2022 the monarch has been King Charles III."),
("Which right does the UK offer everyone living here?",
 "A right to a fair trial", ["A right to free housing", "A right to a public job", "A right to retire at 50"],
 "A right to a fair trial is one of the rights the handbook lists, alongside freedom of belief, freedom of speech and freedom from unfair discrimination. Housing, jobs and retirement age are not rights the handbook promises."),
("According to the handbook, British values are based on:",
 "History and traditions", ["One written constitution", "European Union law", "The rules of one church"],
 "The handbook says British values are based on history and traditions and are protected by law, customs and expectations. The UK has no single written constitution."),
("The handbook says there is no place in British society for:",
 "Extremism or intolerance", ["Different religious beliefs", "Criticism of the government", "Peaceful protest marches"],
 "Extremism and intolerance have no place in British society. Holding different beliefs, criticising the government and protesting peacefully are all part of a free democracy."),
("Alongside obeying the law, the handbook asks everyone who lives in the UK to:",
 "Treat others with fairness", ["Own property in the UK", "Learn a second language", "Join the armed forces"],
 "Treating others with fairness sits alongside obeying the law and respecting others' rights. Owning property, learning another language and joining the forces are not duties."),
("Respecting the rights of others includes respecting their right to:",
 "Their own opinions", ["A share of your income", "Use of your property", "Decide how you vote"],
 "The handbook asks residents to respect the rights of others, including their right to their own opinions. Your income, property and faith remain your own."),
("The principle of the rule of law means that:",
 "Everyone must obey the same laws", ["Only the monarch can make laws", "Judges must follow the government", "Local custom overrides national law"],
 "The rule of law is one of the fundamental principles of British life. Everyone, including people in power, must obey the law, and judges are independent of the government."),
("As well as looking after yourself, the handbook says you should look after:",
 "Your family", ["Your employer", "Your landlord", "Your local MP"],
 "The handbook asks everyone in the UK to look after themselves and their family, alongside obeying the law, respecting others and protecting the environment."),
("Which of these is an example of participation in community life?",
 "Helping at a local charity", ["Watching TV news at home", "Renewing a driving licence", "Paying a council tax bill"],
 "Participation in community life is one of the fundamental principles of British life. Volunteering, for example at a charity or school, is one way to take part and help others."),
("Along with the freedoms of belief and speech, the UK offers everyone a right to join in:",
 "The election of a government", ["The writing of new laws", "The choosing of judges", "The choosing of the monarch"],
 "The handbook lists freedom of belief and religion, freedom of speech, freedom from unfair discrimination, a right to a fair trial and a right to join in the election of a government."),
("Freedom of belief and religion means that people in the UK may:",
 "Follow any faith or none", ["Change faith only once", "Follow only the state church", "Never talk about their faith"],
 "Freedom of belief and religion is one of the freedoms the UK offers everyone. People can follow any religion, change it or have none, and must show tolerance to those who believe differently."),
]
